  "title": "Explore the kant-pastebin codebase to understand the current tile system, plugin architecture, and org-babel capabilities. Specifically:\n\n1. Read the full contents of: src/tiles.rs, src/plugin.rs, src/plugins/mod.rs, src/handlers.rs (especially the paste creation and plugin routes), src/main.rs\n2. Read the org-tile source: tiles/org-tile/src/lib.rs, tiles/org-tile/Cargo.toml\n3. Look at the pastebin routes - how pastes are created, stored, and retrieved\n4. Check if there's any existing org-babel or code execution infrastructure\n5. Check the README-WORKSPACE.md and PASTEBIN_SEMANTICS.md for architecture docs\n\nSummarize the key architecture points:\n- How tiles are loaded and invoked\n- How plugins work vs FFI tiles\n- How pastes flow through the system (create, store, index, retrieve)\n- What org-mode capabilities exist\n- The HTTP API surface",
